# TaskBeacon

TaskBeacon is a small, dependency-minimal command-line task manager written in Python.
It stores tasks in a local JSON file and supports add, list, complete, remove, and search operations.
Designed for quick personal use and as a simple example project to publish on GitHub.

## Features
- Add tasks with optional due date and priority
- List tasks (all / pending / completed)
- Mark tasks complete
- Remove tasks
- Simple text search

## Requirements
- Python 3.8+

## Installation
Clone the repository and install (optional virtual environment recommended):

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/TaskBeacon.git
cd TaskBeacon
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate   # or .venv\Scripts\activate on Windows
pip install -e .
